  <prompt>Port H12bAppConfigSeedHandler.cs's 2 REAL (not stubbed) collaborators: (1) PowerShellAppConfigSeeder(DataGrid) -&gt; seed-reconciliation-gridconfig.ps1 (az account get-access-token + Invoke-RestMethod GET/PATCH/POST on sprk_gridconfigurations); (2) PowerShellAppConfigSeeder(WorkspaceLayout) -&gt; Deploy-SystemWorkspaceLayouts.ps1 (424 lines, 2 az/REST call sites) -- BOTH follow the SAME near-mechanical az-token + Invoke-RestMethod pattern DS-1b characterizes as '~40 lines of Dataverse Web API upsert; near-mechanical port'. Port BOTH to HttpClient + DefaultAzureCredential Web API upserts. This task does NOT touch the 2 DeferredAppConfigSeeder no-op placeholders (field-mapping + chart-def) -- those are task 152's scope (greenfield, not a port).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in near-mechanical Dataverse Web API GET/PATCH/POST porting from short PowerShell scripts.</role>

  <goal>H12bAppConfigSeedHandler.cs's DataGrid and WorkspaceLayout seeder collaborators are pure HttpClient + DefaultAzureCredential Dataverse Web API implementations, replacing their PowerShellAppConfigSeeder script-shells. per-scope seed/verify semantics match the source scripts exactly.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-1b §1 (H12b row, collaborators #23/#24) classifies both as near-mechanical: 'same pattern, ~40 lines of Dataverse Web API upsert; near-mechanical port' for the DataGrid scope, and the identical characterization for WorkspaceLayout. DS-4 §2 (H12b row) classifies H12b overall as PARTIAL -- 'DataGrid + workspace-layout scopes = real pwsh seeders; field-mapping + chart-def scopes = DeferredAppConfigSeeder no-op' -- THIS task addresses only the 2 REAL scopes; task 152 addresses the 2 greenfield gaps.</background>
    <relevant-files>
